<title>FRANCE: France's Giat plans 2,569 job cuts.</title>
<headline>France's Giat plans 2,569 job cuts.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>French armaments group Giat Industries, best known for its the Leclerc tanks, said on Thursday its restructuring plan included 2,569 job cuts out of 12,000, somewhat lower than the 2,741 jobs unions had feared.</p>
<p>The job reductions will include 784 early retirements, 210 voluntary redundancies, 540 workers to be redeployed in the civil service, and 165 to be trained for new jobs.</p>
<p>In a statement following a meeting with the company's central works council, state-owned GIAT also said that measures to reduce working hours could save a thousand jobs.</p>
</text>
